INT. COLD-STORAGE LOCKER, FISH MARKET - NIGHT

Frost on steel. A bare bulb. Three people in a room built for crates of herring.

DETECTIVE RHEA SOLOMON (40s, parka) holds the door ajar with her boot. ARTUR VOSS (50s, soaked suit) stands over an open ice chest. NICO FERRANTE (20s, apron) sits on a pallet, knees up.

SOLOMON
Nobody leaves. Hands where I can see them.

Voss lifts the lid higher. Looks in.

VOSS
(to himself)
Not here. Not here. Where is it.

SOLOMON
Artur. Step back.

VOSS
Nico, did you move it?

NICO
No, sir.

Voss turns. Too fast. Solomon's hand goes to her hip.

SOLOMON
Last warning. Everyone calm down.

NICO
I'm calm. I'm so calm.

The compressor shuts off. Total quiet.

VOSS
(muttering)
Forty years. Forty years.

Voss pulls a hand from his coat. Phone, not a gun. He holds it up like a lantern.

Nico bolts. Solomon spins. The door slams.
